  "details": "VRCInputMethod.Vive is returned for Vive-branded controllers which are not the Vive Wands. This seems to completely miss the point of checking what kind of controllers a user has since Vive Wands specifically have input limitations that need to be detectable so that a script can change how inputs are mapped because they do not have the same number of buttons as nearly all other VR Controllers, and also tend to have different \"analog\" input capabilities.",
